[6] GO2 family vs a physical (lattice) family: who carries the spectrum?
    RETRACTION (draft v1 of this script claimed N_a(E) -> oo at fixed E: FALSE).
    At fixed PHYSICAL energy E, any local QFT at fixed volume has an a-independent
    density of states; free field: N(E) = (L/2pi)^3 (4pi/3) E^3, no a.  The (L/a)^3
    growth sits only at the cutoff scale E ~ 1/a.  So counting does NOT separate
    the two families.  What separates them is WHO carries the a-dependence:
      GO2 (GO2-SOFTMODE.md:66): sigma(H_a) = N_0 u {eps_a}
         -> exactly ONE moving branch; the rest of the spectrum is a-independent.
      physical KS: g^2(a)/2 -> 0 and 1/(2 g^2(a)) -> oo (GO2:162) and the low
         spectrum is a collective property of 9(L/a)^3 link dof (SU(2)).
    link dof count for SU(2), 3 colours x (N^2-1) x (L/a)^3 = 9 (L/a)^3, L=1:
      a=1e-01     links = 9.000e+03      GO2 moving branches = 1
      a=1e-02     links = 9.000e+06      GO2 moving branches = 1
      a=1e-03     links = 9.000e+09      GO2 moving branches = 1
      a=1e-04     links = 9.000e+12      GO2 moving branches = 1
    => the conversion GO2-family -> physical family fails at S2 (rank-one defect
       vs local plaquette sum), NOT at S1 (T-matrix identity, GO2:104 passes).
